{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/948497-deviant-inspirational-charachters-in-other-media","id":948497,"title":"Deviant: Inspirational charachters in other media","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Deviant: The Renegades"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-08-11T04:10:20-07:00","id":948497,"title":"Deviant: Inspirational charachters in other media","content":"Who would you like to be able to recreate in Deviant.<br /> <br /> I'd quite like to play the charachters from Sense8. Power wise they'd be easy, all they need is telepathic communication and the ability to jump into each other's bodies.<br /> <br /> I'd also like to play Penny from the really obscure game The Strangers (it's a mod for the game Freedom Force). She's ageless and can transmute matter into different forms - but finds elements easier than compounds. If she transmutes herself it's always harmless so she could become solid metal for toughness or turn into gas for intangibility. She also has a symbiotic and loyal ephemeral being that lives in her body, which she can send out on errands. It's extremely fast and can transmute matter like she can, but it's causes atomic instability if it gets too far from her body.<br /> <br /> Chaos' Conspiracy: <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Is actually the science superhero who created her. In his civilian identity he was working on a cure for Penny's rare form of cancer, but after too much time fighting evil he mixed up the medicine with a vial of demon blood and injected it directly into Penny's cancer. The result caused it to transform into a loyal symbiotic ephemeral being. This saved Penny's life from cancer, granted her top-tier super powers, and possibly agelessness.<br /> <br /> Naturally Penny's was ecstatic but her creator is convinced he's ruined her life and is trying to cure her. Unlike the superhero verse of The Strangers, in Deviant he'd have a good reason to want to cure Penny. </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-11T08:21:24-07:00","id":948621,"title":"","content":"Provided the variability of things haven't been overstated, it looks like you will be able to create a huge number of comic book and video game characters. As well as most powered people from 90s sci-fi movies.<br /> <br /> I wouldn't be surprised if you could make versions of the other supernatural lines, like vampires and sin-eaters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-11T20:48:22-07:00","id":949071,"title":"","content":"Well, the whole &quot;Deviant&quot; subgenre was sort of started with Dr. Jekyll and Mr. Hyde and The Invisible Man. <br /> <br /> My favorite currently running Deviant stories are Orphan Black and Stranger Things, both of which Dave explicitly called out as inspirations- he even said he'd be statting up 11 himself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-11T21:22:02-07:00","id":949094,"title":"","content":"The eponymous facility from <i>Dollhouse</i> is a pretty textbook Deviant Org, as is the Alliance reseach lab that screwed with River in <i>Firefly</i>, and of course, the Watchers from <i>Buffy</i>.<br /> <br /> Hang on. Are we sure that Joss Whedon isn't the one developing this game?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-11T21:25:15-07:00","id":949097,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/948497-deviant-inspirational-charachters-in-other-media?p=949094#post949094\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The eponymous facility from <i>Dollhouse</i> is a pretty textbook Deviant Org, as is the Alliance reseach lab that screwed with River in <i>Firefly</i>, and of course, the Watchers from <i>Buffy</i>.<br /> <br /> Hang on. Are we sure that Joss Whedon isn't the one developing this game?</div> </div> </div> </div>*involuntary shudder*","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-12T01:48:59-07:00","id":949194,"title":"","content":"Midnight Special wasn't a particularly great film (the first half was good though). But it is an interesting and unique one, and it's definitely a Deviant story.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-12T11:01:21-07:00","id":949422,"title":"","content":"Tetsuo: The Iron Man was mentioned as another source of inspiration, and that was what got me really excited for it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-12T16:27:21-07:00","id":949608,"title":"","content":"More recently in upcoming stuff, Marvel/Netflix's Luke Cage series comes to mind. Not entirely sure if they would go the angle of Luke getting back at the guys who put him on the slab, but still.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-14T21:06:40-07:00","id":950898,"title":"","content":"Metal Gear. Between the conspiracies and the <b><i>SCIENCE!</i></b>, Deviant definitely needs Metal Gear.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-14T21:42:21-07:00","id":950915,"title":"","content":"Snow Flame! Cocaine is his god, and he is the human instrument of Her will! <br /> <br /> He's an obscure dc villain that showed up in a single issue of New Guardians, and then again in a fan comic that was pretty great. He is a drug trafficker that is possessed by a powerful spirit which is itself a servant of the god Cocaine. He's an enthusiastic guy, with a lot of energy and a priestly desire to see his gods' influence spread across Gotham, even if it means clashing with the JL to get it done.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><br /> I draw things! Wanna check it out? Click on the link below!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.deviantart.com/jordantroy\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.deviantart.com/jordantroy</a><br /> <br /> <i><b>YES! I do commissions! </b></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/848-jtroy","name":"JTroy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar848_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-18T12:24:57-07:00","id":953347,"title":"","content":"I happen to think that video game protagonists are a massive source for inspiration- you were normal and then BAM! you aren't happens a lot in video games.<br /> <br /> Megaman, Alex Mercer, Torque, bioshock protagonists, etc, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-18T13:04:01-07:00","id":953370,"title":"","content":"Eleven from Stranger Things would very likely fit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5557-runcible","name":"Runcible","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5557_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"164"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-18T13:40:47-07:00","id":953401,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StSword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/948497-deviant-inspirational-charachters-in-other-media?p=953347#post953347\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I happen to think that video game protagonists are a massive source for inspiration- you were normal and then BAM! you aren't happens a lot in video games.<br /> <br /> Megaman, Alex Mercer, Torque, bioshock protagonists, etc, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wasn't Megaman(Rockman) a custom built Android, though?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-18T14:58:58-07:00","id":953440,"title":"","content":"Honestly, when I first heard about Deviant and what it's about, the first thing to come to my mind was Kamen Rider. Then, IIRC, somewhere it was mentioned, among other inspirations like Hulk, that Guyver was an inspirational media for the game. I'm a huge fan of Bio-Booster Armor Guyver so I think I'ma goin to try to make a Kamen Rider/Guyver-like character.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/427-rahuman101","name":"Rahuman101","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar427_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-18T17:14:22-07:00","id":953496,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/948497-deviant-inspirational-charachters-in-other-media?p=953401#post953401\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Wasn't Megaman(Rockman) a custom built Android, though?</div> </div> </div> </div> Yes and no.<br /> <br /> Yes, he's an android.<br /> <br /> No, he wasn't built for superheroics, he was altered for superheroics.<br /> <br /> He was built to be a lab assistant. When the other robots were corrupted, he volunteered to be changed into megaman.<br /> <br /> At least, if one is talking about classic megaman. Other iterations have included such beings as a boy possessed by an electromagnetic alien, a dead boy being converted into a virtual lifeform, or a child merged with a nanotech symbiote. <br /> <br /> Androids was treated as a mere origin, worthy of a 1-5 group of merits, but so was being born rich, poor, or being bridge and tunnel in Bleeding Edge, the cyberpunk supplement. <br /> <br /> Promethean treated three law compliant robots as a thing in the nwod, even without the divine fire, in fact especially without the divine fire, because it said that any such programming restrictions went away when a machine becomes a promethean. <br /> <br /> And &quot;in vitro&quot; is considered a valid origin for Deviants, so some deviants were never normal to begin with.<br /> <br /> Now certainly a ST can veto an android deviant in their games, but such would not contradict the setting, the rules, or the basic premise of the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-18T17:16:36-07:00","id":953497,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tiresias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/948497-deviant-inspirational-charachters-in-other-media?p=950898#post950898\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Metal Gear. Between the conspiracies and the <b><i>SCIENCE!</i></b>, Deviant definitely needs Metal Gear.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed,<br /> <br /> The Metal Gear Mythos is stuffed to the brim with Empowered but Doomed individuals, Sinister Organizations, Labyrinthine Conspiracies, and Twisted Science. And the music from Metal Gear Rising: Revengeance is pretty much the soundtrack for a Deviants Chronicle!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-18T18:36:16-07:00","id":953557,"title":"","content":"<div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><img src=\"http://i.imgur.com/RAeDFx2.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I imagine in terms of Deviants-from-birth they'll still be wanted by an organization or individual, however that turns out.<br /> <br /> Honestly I prefer there to be no real Golconda-like blessing that 'cures' you or somehow washes away all the bad while letting you keep all the good, but we'll see what they come up with. If there was an 'end,' I'd probably prefer it to be something like Laird Barron's <a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Light-Darkness-Laird-Barron-ebook/dp/B008RDKN7W/\" target=\"_blank\">The Light is the Darkness</a>, where one takes their powers as far as they can go and are no longer a Deviant because they're no longer a recognizable part of the race, religion or society they've deviated from. It's sort of falls in line with the myths of more of the other games.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 08-18-2016, 09:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-20T01:35:43-07:00","id":954274,"title":"","content":"I want to be the main protagonist of a grim and gritty inspector gadget reboot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-21T14:40:55-07:00","id":955188,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reighnhell</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/948497-deviant-inspirational-charachters-in-other-media?p=953497#post953497\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Agreed,<br /> <br /> The Metal Gear Mythos is stuffed to the brim with Empowered but Doomed individuals, Sinister Organizations, Labyrinthine Conspiracies, and Twisted Science. And the music from Metal Gear Rising: Revengeance is pretty much the soundtrack for a Deviants Chronicle!</div> </div> </div> </div>Definitely. Interestingly, Revengeance is overwhelmingly pro-transhumanism (one of the things I loved about it), while even I wouldn't want Deviant to be that positive, being that it's a horror game and all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-23T02:40:43-07:00","id":1143183,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rahuman101</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/948497-deviant-inspirational-charachters-in-other-media?p=953440#post953440\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, when I first heard about Deviant and what it's about, the first thing to come to my mind was Kamen Rider. Then, IIRC, somewhere it was mentioned, among other inspirations like Hulk, that Guyver was an inspirational media for the game. I'm a huge fan of Bio-Booster Armor Guyver so I think I'ma goin to try to make a Kamen Rider/Guyver-like character.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think something like Kamen Rider Amazons would be especially fitting for Deviant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/17107-mangaholic13","name":"Mangaholic13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar17107_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-23T12:16:22-07:00","id":1143291,"title":"","content":"Any media example of a magical deviant rather than one made by mad science? The only example I know is the original Slayer from Buffy. Maybe Opress Savage too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-23T18:05:11-07:00","id":1143367,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Raistlin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/948497-deviant-inspirational-charachters-in-other-media?p=1143291#post1143291\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Any media example of a magical deviant rather than one made by mad science? The only example I know is the original Slayer from Buffy. Maybe Opress Savage too.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ashitaka and his cursed, super-strong arm from Princess Mononoke.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Sure, he was cured by the Forest Spirit, but that thing was probably a Rank 6+ entity who could pull off stuff like removing Major Templates.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":7920,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","user":"Master Aquatosic","date":". 09-24-2017, 11:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-23T22:44:19-07:00","id":1143407,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Raistlin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/948497-deviant-inspirational-charachters-in-other-media?p=1143291#post1143291\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Any media example of a magical deviant rather than one made by mad science? The only example I know is the original Slayer from Buffy. Maybe Opress Savage too.</div> </div> </div> </div>Raven, from Teen Titans. Spawn. Witchblade, the Darkness. The manga and anime of <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Claymore_(manga)\" target=\"_blank\">Claymore</a>, Blue Exorcist, Naruto.<br /> <br /> Yes, there's overlap with other game lines, but that seems to be part of their selling point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-24T08:04:36-07:00","id":1143458,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/948497-deviant-inspirational-charachters-in-other-media?p=1143407#post1143407\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Naruto.<br /> Yes, there's overlap with other game lines, but that seems to be part of their selling point.</div> </div> </div> </div>Naruto is pretty powerful for a Deviant","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-24T14:24:39-07:00","id":1143589,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Raistlin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/948497-deviant-inspirational-charachters-in-other-media?p=1143291#post1143291\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Any media example of a magical deviant rather than one made by mad science? The only example I know is the original Slayer from Buffy. Maybe Opress Savage too.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bThe Jinchuriki in Naruto. The Magatama that fuse with the protagonist's body in Shin Megami Tenshi: Nocturne. I think there was something similar in the anime Blue Seed but it's been a long time since I've seen that one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1869-moonwolf8","name":"moonwolf8","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-24T16:12:49-07:00","id":1143618,"title":"","content":"Spawn, the Darkness and Alex Mercer sound really, really cool.<br /> (If you go Spawn, you definitly have to have that part where a Vampire convinces the homeless who Al protects that Al is a Vampire, and so they turn on him. Ahhh, classic. One of the first issues I read.)<br /> <br /> Also, just because it was a bad movie does not mean one should not mention Chronicle here, right? =D<br /> Somehow, I also have to think of the Breath of Fire game, I think 4, with Fou Lu, where a summoning ceremony went wrong, and a Dragon God was split into two entities that arrived at different times. Both fight the empire Fou Lu created some centuries ago on some occasions and for different reasons.<br /> <br /> You could go Rocksteady and Bepop, Splinter or outright Ninja Turtles.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-28T17:29:08-07:00","id":1145027,"title":"","content":"Could Assassin's Creed be interpreted as a city-level/global-level Deviant game?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-29T00:36:59-07:00","id":1145122,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Haberdasher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/948497-deviant-inspirational-charachters-in-other-media?p=1145027#post1145027\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Could Assassin's Creed be interpreted as a city-level/global-level Deviant game?</div> </div> </div> </div>I still thinks of AC as Sleepwalkers-level Mage game, where Assasins are coalition of Diamond Orders and Templars are part of Seers of Throne - both groups fighting over mystical 'Pieces of Eden' Artifacts from Time Before. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-29T06:23:18-07:00","id":1145198,"title":"","content":"The Ace of Spades, the mad scientist who inspired <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1125752-variations-question-modular-option\">this question</a>, is based primarily on Osamu Tezuka's Black Jack (though the proposed Variations mentioned in that thread-starter were suggested by his other main inspiration, Mayuri Kurotsuchi from <i>BLEACH</i>).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1426-aberranteyes","name":"AberrantEyes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1426_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-30T21:44:17-07:00","id":1145715,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Raistlin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/948497-deviant-inspirational-charachters-in-other-media?p=1143291#post1143291\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Any media example of a magical deviant rather than one made by mad science? The only example I know is the original Slayer from Buffy. Maybe Opress Savage too.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maria from South of Hell is strictly speaking a demoniac, but could be rendered as a deviant pretty easily. The demon was put in her by a cult - to Deviant-ise, have the possession catastrophically fail, break open Maria's soul, and create the secondary personality of Abigail - with variations of enhanced strength and an ability to chew on spirits, and a scar of an inhuman appearance (all of which can be suppressed) - and also a scar that sometimes Abigail will manifest to Maria and the two can kvetch at each other.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-17T12:51:45-07:00","id":1520832,"title":"","content":"So my brother has a history of making characters based off video games and such.<br /> <br /> <b>Jackie Estacado</b><br /> Or more specifically\u2026<br /> The Darkness.<br /> <br /> I think I made it right as far as the game is concerned. Here\u2019s what I got:<br /> <br /> origin: Exomorph AKA Unwilling<br /> Clade: Chimeric<br /> <br /> Telekinesis 4 (the extra limbs)<br /> deviations: throw, crush<br /> Scar: Monstrous transformation <br /> <br /> Carapace 4<br /> deviations: Bulletproof, Dense, Flak<br /> Scar: Monstrous Transformation <br /> <br /> Monstrous Transformation 4<br /> Links Telekinesis AND Carapace together<br /> Scar: Power Failure<br /> <br /> Power Failure 4<br /> Trigger: Bright Lights. <br /> (deactivates/locks \u2018darkness powers\u2019 until end of scene)<br /> <br /> Integrate Technology 3<br /> Scar; Tribulation<br /> (Mainly allows him to fire his guns as if they have unlimited ammo)<br /> <br /> tribulation 3<br /> costs 1 willpower to use<br /> (To keep the \u2018wannabe merciless gunman\u2019 power at bay)<br /> <br /> Rapid healing 2<br /> Scar: Noticable, +1 free overt<br /> heals 1B per turn, all bashing at end of scene, removes colds, food poisoning, sprains.<br /> (Not entirely sure if this is a \u2018legal build\u2019, not entirely \u2018required\u2019 for the darkness feel)<br /> <br /> <br /> and just in case, a 2 dot scar<br /> Alternate Persona 2<br /> Deviations: Aware<br /> (represents the darkness watching from inside)<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> And that\u2019s it. 9 dots. Dunno if I made it all correctly or not, but in my opinion it\u2019s a good idea in the sense of \u201chere\u2019s something you can add to any character you want.<br /> No need for merits, nor any minimum attribute requirements. <br /> <br /> Let me know how you like it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28143-firestar001","name":"firestar001","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}